  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The project aims to enhance security and accessibility using AI. Key milestones include a call for R&D ideas by July 20th, initial findings of a potential 20% efficiency increase discussed on August 5th, and team expansions adding members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing. The project moved from design to development under lead developer Omar Jensen, celebrated the completion of the testing phase on October 10th, and is currently seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November. Additionally, a $15,000 training budget has been approved for the coding team and project managers."
